  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/SW17-M35-0B6C77913DB3">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>SW17-M35-0B6C77913DB3</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified) — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Optical input through the SMA fibre connector; acquisition integration time, averaging and trigger selection from the host PC over USB or serial connection. USB provides power. Normal/free-run, external synchronous, external hardware-level and external hardware-edge triggering are documented. DD4 pin 2 accepts the external TTL trigger (5 or 3.3 V as specified); GPIO pins are not 5 V tolerant. Exact Flame-S/Flame-T detector, slit and wavelength configuration is unspecified in this row.
Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Wavelength-resolved spectra and derived absorbance/reflectance/emission through the host software, subject to calibration. Red LED steady=powered; green LED steady=ready and flashing=acquiring. Single/continuous strobe, lamp-enable, configurable GPIO and serial transmit are documented at the DD4 interface. Pin voltages/directions vary; refer to the pin table rather than treating every signal as 5 V TTL.
Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>nm (wavelength/resolution); µm (slit width); µs, ms and s (integration/trigger timing); Hz (scan rate); V and mA (electrical interface/power); detector counts and configured logic states (dimensionless). Detector-specific integration ranges must not be merged between Flame-S and Flame-T.
Source: Manuals/Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)__linked-manual__aa2aa40792.pdf, PDF pp. 12, 15, 21–26, 35, 55, 59–61, 65–67.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>738</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Ocean Optics Flame spectrometer (configuration unspecified)</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://www.oceanoptics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Flame-User-Manual.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
