  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M32-01">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>M32-01</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Bronkhorst EL-FLOW Select F-200CV — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Compatible gas, electrical supply and flow setpoint. EL-FLOW Select family manual describes analog/digital remote control and RS-232; other fieldbus interfaces depend on the ordered option. Normally-closed and normally-open valve constructions are alternatives, not interchangeable states of every unit. F-200CV-specific full-scale range is not established here.
Source: H, PDF pp. 8–11 (EL-FLOW Select family).</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Measured/controlled gas flow plus diagnostics, alarms and counters; analog/digital communication depends on the ordered interface. Exact scaling, valve option and complete signal-state map require the serial-label configuration.
Source: H, PDF pp. 8–11 (EL-FLOW Select family).</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>mLₙ/min and Lₙ/min (normalized gas flow); bar (pressure). Other interface units/scaling are configuration-dependent.
Source: H, PDF pp. 8–11 (EL-FLOW Select family).</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>165</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Bronkhorst EL-FLOW Select F-200CV</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://products.bronkhorst.com/media/3u4iwfxh/917099-manual-el-flow-select.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
