  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M12-02">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>M12-02</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>FRITSCH PULVERISETTE 7 premium line — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Grinding feed and media: Organic/inorganic samples; grinding bowls and balls selected for feed material; states: Dry grinding or wet grinding; media/compatibility are configuration-dependent; phase: Dry solid, emulsion or suspension as specified
Mains input: 100–240 V ±10%; approx. 10 A at 115 V or 5 A at 230 V; maximum power approximately 1100 W; states: Mains off/on; voltage-change procedure and restart protection apply
Program parameters: Speed up to 1100 rpm; time up to 999 min; pause up to 99 min; cycles up to 99; states: Numeric program entries; starts only after bowl/closing checks
Cover and bowl sensing: Sensors check grinding bowls and cover mechanism; states: Bowl detected/not detected; stationary-drive/cover conditions; safety checks before starting
Additional documented controls/states: lid opening/locking control.
Source: Manuals/FRITSCH PULVERISETTE 7 premium line__linked-manual__34deccc603.pdf, PDF p. 18.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Ground sample: Manual reports dry d50 &lt;20 µm and wet d50 &lt;0.1 µm depending on material; states: Ground material; actual size requires measurement and depends on process; phase: Dry powder or wet suspension
Operating/fault indication: Display signals overload; drive stops for overheating, blockage or excessive imbalance; states: Grinding; paused/stopped; reduced-speed overload; thermal/blockage/imbalance shutdown; no automatic restart after power loss</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>A; V; W; cycle count; mL; min; mm; rpm; state; µm</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
