  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment/MIT-M38-31B34079E2C9">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#EquipmentModel"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/ProductModel"/>
    <dct:identifier>MIT-M38-31B34079E2C9</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>RAITH VELION</rdfs:label>
    <dct:isPartOf rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/dataset/equipment"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment.csv"/>
    <schema:name>RAITH VELION</schema:name>
    <schema:model>RAITH VELION</schema:model>
    <icon:inCategory rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M38"/>
    <schema:category rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/category/M38"/>
    <icon:manufacturer rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/manufacturer/raith"/>
    <schema:manufacturer rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/manufacturer/raith"/>
    <icon:recordKind>facility_documented_model</icon:recordKind>
    <icon:variantLabel>VELION</icon:variantLabel>
    <icon:modelStatus>facility_documented_model</icon:modelStatus>
    <icon:manualStatus>technical_specification_available</icon:manualStatus>
    <icon:priceStatus>no_public_exact_msrp_confirmed</icon:priceStatus>
    <icon:relatedMaterialTypes>Nanofilms and nanoscale coatings</icon:relatedMaterialTypes>
    <icon:relatedProcessTypes>Lithography and nanopattern fabrication</icon:relatedProcessTypes>
    <icon:associationBasis>Existing ontology class used as optional process characterization/quality-control equipment; this does not make this model a source-paper apparatus or universal production requirement. FIB machining capability does not make this an EBL writer or an ion-implantation system; M38 covers its SEM channel only.</icon:associationBasis>
    <icon:reviewDate>2026-10-17</icon:reviewDate>
    <icon:notes>FIB-SEM uses ion species such asAu/Ge/Si for direct milling, plus an FE-SEM column for process control. It is not electron-beam resist lithography M59. Existing M61 source class/subtypes currently cover reactive-ion/plasma and wet etching, so a dedicated FIB nanopatterning class/route would be needed before offering its ion-writing function. RAITH uppercase is the already-verified canonical manufacturer key; separate Raith row should not cause unverified display.  Exact-model official technical product page; an operator manual was not independently located. No verified current US machine purchase price. Facility usage rates are excluded. Optional characterization candidates do not change required process steps.</icon:notes>
    <icon:catalogScope>mit_nano_expansion</icon:catalogScope>
    <icon:manualMatchStatus>not_verified</icon:manualMatchStatus>
    <icon:modelEvidenceStatus>documented</icon:modelEvidenceStatus>
    <icon:imageScope>Current official VELION product photograph; installed MIT options may differ. Source image rights remain with the originating facility/manufacturer.</icon:imageScope>
    <icon:mediaCheckedDate>2026-10-17</icon:mediaCheckedDate>
    <icon:productPageScope>Official model or model-family information; historical model/configuration is separately documented by MIT.nano.</icon:productPageScope>
    <icon:equipmentSubtype>SEM inspection only; FIB milling is separate</icon:equipmentSubtype>
