  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-05">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>M07-05</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>New Era NE-4000 — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Sample feed: Material in compatible syringe; chemical compatibility depends on syringe and tubing; states: Loaded syringe; material composition not prescribed; phase: Fluid; phase/composition not comprehensively specified
DC power: 12 V DC; 1000 mA at full load; states: Power connected or disconnected; country-specific external adapter
Syringe internal diameter: 0.100–50.00 mm; states: Numeric setting; syringe-specific
Flow-rate setting: 1.436 µL/h with 1 mL B-D syringe to 6023 mL/h with 60 mL B-D syringe (manual edition); states: Numeric rate; syringe-dependent limits
Dispense target and direction: VOL target; DIR INF/WDR/REV/STK; states: Infuse, withdraw, reverse or sticky direction; target volume is numeric
Program definition: Up to 41 phases; phase functions include rate, fill, increment/decrement, stop, jump, loop, pause, conditional/event and output functions; states: RAT/FIL/INC/DEC/STP/JMP/PRI/PRL/LPS/LOP/LPE/PAS/IF/EVN/EVS/EVR/CLD/TRG/BEP/OUT; details depend on firmware
Operational trigger, pin 2: TTL LOW 0–1.5 V; HIGH 3.5–5.25 V; stable level ≥100 ms; states: FT/FH/F2/LE/ST/T2/SP/P2/RL/RH/SL/SH/OF; event-trap modes ET/BT also documented; edge meaning is mode-dependent
Direction input, pin 3: TTL LOW 0–1.5 V; HIGH 3.5–5.25 V; states: dr:rE: falling edge infuse, rising edge withdraw; dr:dU reverses that mapping
Event and program inputs, pins 4 and 6: TTL LOW 0–1.5 V; HIGH 3.5–5.25 V; states: Pin 4 event/user input; pin 6 conditional or user input, also keypad lockout
RS-232 commands and responses: 300/1200/2400/9600/19200 baud; up to 100 pumps; states: Commands RUN/STP/PUR; DIS/VER/IN queries; status/error responses; basic or safe communications mode</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>RS-232 commands and responses: 300/1200/2400/9600/19200 baud; up to 100 pumps; states: Commands RUN/STP/PUR; DIS/VER/IN queries; status/error responses; basic or safe communications mode
Dispensed/withdrawn material: Flow follows the configured direction and syringe-dependent rate; states: Infusing, withdrawing or stopped; phase: Fluid; phase/composition depends on loaded sample
Program output, pin 5: User/program-defined logic output; states: LOW or HIGH; OUT 5 {0|1}
Motor-running output, pin 7: RUN.0 or RUN.1 mapping; states: RUN.0 HIGH=pumping, LOW=not pumping; RUN.1 HIGH=pumping or pause timer, LOW=program stopped/paused
Direction output, pin 8: Logic direction indication; states: HIGH=infuse; LOW=withdraw
Dispensed-volume/status response: DIS reports dispensed volume; firmware/status responses available through RS-232; states: Separate infuse/withdraw counters; status responses depend on command and pump state
Buzzer: BUZ controls audible notification; states: Off, continuous, or specified number of beeps</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>V; baud; beep count; logic level; mA; mL; mL/h; mL/hr; mL/min; mm; ms; phase count; pump count; s; µL; µL/h; µL/hr; µL/min</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>726</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>New Era NE-4000</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://www.syringepump.com/download/NE-4000%20Syringe%20Pump%20User%20Manual.pdf"/>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://www.syringepump.com/NE-4000.php"/>
