    <icon:inputDescription>Powder/material in a selected pressing die; hand-operated separate hydraulic pump and cylinder. Transparent safety cover; optional electric/programmed pumps are separate configurations, not base-model controls. The source contains conflicting cylinder-travel figures, so no travel limit is assigned.
Source: I, YLJ-24TS specifications and gauge-to-force conversion.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Pressed sample/compact and built-in hydraulic-pressure gauge indication. Applied force is calculated from the listed gauge conversion; the base press does not itself report a digital sample-force signal. No electrical/data-output states are specified.
Source: I, YLJ-24TS specifications and gauge-to-force conversion.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>MPa (gauge pressure); metric tonne-force (applied force convention); mm/cm (die/cylinder geometry); °C (operating environment). m/s² appears only as a gravity constant in the conversion formula.
Source: I, YLJ-24TS specifications and gauge-to-force conversion.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
