    <icon:associationBasis>Broad-beam UHV RF ion-source family; source component for processing/deposition, not whole turnkey vacuum system. Manufacturer product claims only. P/N links express curator relevance, not source-article apparatus, measured performance, exact host compatibility or mandatory process steps.</icon:associationBasis>
    <icon:reviewDate>2026-10-18</icon:reviewDate>
    <icon:notes>The page uses both TAS RFI and TASRI Series; retained as aliases for one series-level entry, not two numbered models. Image shows exposed source internals at family scope. The page links an atom-source brochure, which is excluded as a mismatched ion document. P14 relevance is an ion-beam etching configuration, not equivalence to RIE or a complete etch system. Public purchase price and exact-model operating manual were not published in this bounded review. No documented successor relationship or newest-generation claim. No make/model match in the user-designated Purdue list; generic PVD wording is not asset identity.</icon:notes>
    <icon:catalogScope>manufacturer_catalog</icon:catalogScope>
    <icon:manualMatchStatus>manufacturer_specification</icon:manualMatchStatus>
    <icon:modelEvidenceStatus>documented</icon:modelEvidenceStatus>
    <icon:imageScope>Manufacturer Photograph: Real exposed ion-source hardware close-up showing perforated grid and copper coil. RF ion family; no readable exact model identifier. Source internals/detail; not complete packaged system. Rights reserved; linked official asset.</icon:imageScope>
    <icon:mediaCheckedDate>2026-10-18</icon:mediaCheckedDate>
    <icon:productPageScope>Broad-beam UHV RF ion-source family; source component for processing/deposition, not whole turnkey vacuum system. Manufacturer product claims only. P/N links express curator relevance, not source-article apparatus, measured performance, exact host compatibility or mandatory process steps.</icon:productPageScope>
