    <icon:inputDescription>Sample aerosol through the flow path and surrounding desiccant (or activated charcoal for the described solvent-vapour application). Coalescing preseparator collects large droplets. -NC identifies cobalt-free desiccant; no electronic control inputs are listed.
Source: I, PDF p. 39, Diffusion Dryers 3062 &amp; 3062-NC.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Aerosol with reduced moisture/solvent vapour; collected large droplets in the preseparator. Aerosol does not contact the desiccant. No sensor/data output or discrete electrical states are specified.
Source: I, PDF p. 39, Diffusion Dryers 3062 &amp; 3062-NC.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>L/min (maximum aerosol flow); °C (external desiccant-regeneration temperature, not a dryer temperature setpoint)
Source: I, PDF p. 39, Diffusion Dryers 3062 &amp; 3062-NC.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
