    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <dct:identifier>CAT-EV-7FAFF2F17D36A95E</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Theris identifies Theris TAS RFI / TASRI series in its official product documentation.</rdfs:label>
    <icon:claim>Theris identifies Theris TAS RFI / TASRI series in its official product documentation.</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>curator_reviewed_catalog</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>Broad-beam UHV RF ion-source family; source component for processing/deposition, not whole turnkey vacuum system. Manufacturer product claims only. P/N links express curator relevance, not source-article apparatus, measured performance, exact host compatibility or mandatory process steps. The page uses both TAS RFI and TASRI Series; retained as aliases for one series-level entry, not two numbered models. Image shows exposed source internals at family scope. The page links an atom-source brochure, which is excluded as a mismatched ion document. P14 relevance is an ion-beam etching configuration, not equivalence to RIE or a complete etch system. Public purchase price and exact-model operating manual were not published in this bounded review. No documented successor relationship or newest-generation claim. No make/model match in the user-designated Purdue list; generic PVD wording is not asset identity.</icon:scope>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://therisnano.com/tas-rf-ion-sources/"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/CAT-EV-7FAFF2F17D36A95E%3A1"/>
  </rdf:Description>
