    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <dct:identifier>IMG-EV-58CF2AB92ADAC6CD</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>The linked source presents an instrument photograph matched to RETSCH PM 400 (exact model).</rdfs:label>
    <icon:claim>The linked source presents an instrument photograph matched to RETSCH PM 400 (exact model).</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>curator_reviewed_media</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>Manufacturer photograph of RETSCH PM 400. Options and accessories may vary. Official PM400 model page main instrument image; PM400 is the four-station floor model. Remote image reference; source rights are retained. The photograph does not establish an installed asset, delivered configuration, price, operating procedure or experimental validation.</icon:scope>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://www.retsch.com/products/milling/ball-mills/planetary-ball-mill-pm-400/"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/IMG-EV-58CF2AB92ADAC6CD%3A1"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence/CAT-EV-AAF0839A71FB80EA">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#SourceEvidence"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
    <dct:identifier>CAT-EV-AAF0839A71FB80EA</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Theris identifies Theris TAS30 in its official product documentation.</rdfs:label>
    <icon:claim>Theris identifies Theris TAS30 in its official product documentation.</icon:claim>
    <icon:classification>curator_reviewed_catalog</icon:classification>
    <icon:scope>UHV RF atom-source components for atomic species deposition/cleaning; not turnkey vacuum systems. Manufacturer product claims only. P/N links express curator relevance, not source-article apparatus, measured performance, exact host compatibility or mandatory process steps. TAS atom brochure pages 2 and 4 identify the 30 mm aperture variant. Neutral-atom source for a compatible host, distinct from the ion-source series. P19 relevance is specifically an optional nitride-PLD configuration; not apparatus from the cited P19 experiment. P46 relevance does not establish a replacement for UCLA installed hardware. Manufacturer operating envelopes are not recipe setpoints. Public purchase price and exact-model operating manual were not published in this bounded review. No documented successor relationship or newest-generation claim. No make/model match in the user-designated Purdue list; generic PVD wording is not asset identity.</icon:scope>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://therisnano.com/rf-atom-sources/"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://therisnano.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/TAS-Brochure-2023.pdf"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/CAT-EV-AAF0839A71FB80EA%3A1"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/CAT-EV-AAF0839A71FB80EA%3A2"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M14-01%3Ainputs_and_states">
