  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M34-09%3Ainputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Input and input states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>inputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Nanoparticle suspension/solution in the appropriate cell. Particle sizing requires 0.9 mL in the standard cell or 20 µL in the micro-volume cell; zeta analysis requires 0.7 mL in a standard glass cell or 130 µL in a disposable cell. Peltier temperature control is specified from 0 to 90 °C. The ELSZ-PT pH/additive autotitrator and surface-zeta accessory are optional, not assumed installed. The brochure does not provide the command, trigger or ready/alarm state map.
Source: Manuals/Otsuka-ELSZ2000-brochure-Hi-Res.pdf, PDF pp. 9–11, visually reviewed.</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M34-09"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/EXT-M84-988C964A08CA">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>EXT-M84-988C964A08CA</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Q 400 D — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Hot workpiece and oil or water bath; combination D models have separate oil/water compartments. Manual charging or optional charging aids/coolers/heaters depend on the ordered setup. A lid, supply and drain connections are described; the catalog does not enumerate an electrical state machine.
Source: I, PDF p. 86, Quenching and Cleaning Baths model table.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Quenched/cooled workpiece. The catalog specifies bath capacity/load and optional cooling/heating equipment, not measured microstructure, a logged cooling curve or signal-output states.
Source: I, PDF p. 86, Quenching and Cleaning Baths model table.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>L (bath volume); kg (load); kg/h (quenching performance). Optional accessories use °C, V, kW and, for the stated pneumatic charging aid, bar.
Source: I, PDF p. 86, Quenching and Cleaning Baths model table.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>705</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Nabertherm Q 400 D</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://nabertherm.com/sites/default/files/2023-08/thermalprocesstechnology2_english.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M41-04%3Aunits_of_measure">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Measuring units</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>units_of_measure</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>µm (size/displacement); °C (temperature); nm (wavelength/size); Hz (frequency); min (time); h (time); V (electrical voltage); kHz (frequency); µA (electrical current); µL (volume); mm (travel/size); MHz (frequency)
Source: Manuals/Cypher-AFM-Family-Brochure.pdf, PDF pp. 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 14, 16.</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M41-04"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-026%3Ainputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Input and input states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>inputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Payloads/end effectors for two FR3 arms and the mobile base; teleoperation or learned-policy commands through the integrated software. The manufacturer sheet lists 3 kg payload per arm, 100 kg base payload, maximum base speed 1.75 m/s and 1 kHz FCI. Wi-Fi, Ethernet, USB and Bluetooth are listed. Installed controller commands, safety-state guards and utility/power ratings are not enumerated in this two-page sheet.
Source: I, Mobile FR3 Duo manufacturer sheet, PDF pp. 1–2.</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-026"/>
  </rdf:Description>
