  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/EXT-M84-D5BA4C1D7090">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>EXT-M84-D5BA4C1D7090</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Q 200 D — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Hot workpiece and oil or water bath; combination D models have separate oil/water compartments. Manual charging or optional charging aids/coolers/heaters depend on the ordered setup. A lid, supply and drain connections are described; the catalog does not enumerate an electrical state machine.
Source: I, PDF p. 86, Quenching and Cleaning Baths model table.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Quenched/cooled workpiece. The catalog specifies bath capacity/load and optional cooling/heating equipment, not measured microstructure, a logged cooling curve or signal-output states.
Source: I, PDF p. 86, Quenching and Cleaning Baths model table.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>L (bath volume); kg (load); kg/h (quenching performance). Optional accessories use °C, V, kW and, for the stated pneumatic charging aid, bar.
Source: I, PDF p. 86, Quenching and Cleaning Baths model table.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>704</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Nabertherm Q 200 D</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://nabertherm.com/sites/default/files/2023-08/thermalprocesstechnology2_english.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M40-09%3Aoutputs_and_states">
