    <rdfs:label>Agilent Cary 100 — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Sample/reference in appropriate UV-Vis cells or installed solid-sample accessories; wavelength scan, variable slit width, signal averaging/integration and photometric method. Temperature-controlled cell hardware and reflectance/film accessories are options, not assumed installed. The brochure identifies Cary 100 operation at 190–900 nm; electrical/control-state maps are not provided.
Source: Manuals/Agilent Cary 100.pdf, PDF pp. 2, 4–10.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Absorbance/transmittance versus wavelength; kinetics and optional accessory-dependent reflectance, film or colour analysis. The Cary 100 working absorbance range is described as beyond 4 Abs; the Cary 300’s 6 Abs claim is not assigned to this row.
Source: Manuals/Agilent Cary 100.pdf, PDF pp. 2, 4–10.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>nm (wavelength and spectral resolution); Abs/AU (absorbance, dimensionless); % (transmission/reflectance); °C (optional cell-temperature control).
Source: Manuals/Agilent Cary 100.pdf, PDF pp. 2, 4–10.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
