    <icon:inputDescription>The linked source is the MultiPort cell kit: electrolyte, a metal working-electrode specimen, graphite counter electrode and a separately selected reference electrode. Optional purge/blanket gas requires a vent; the cell is not a pressure vessel. Optional jacket accepts circulating bath fluid; spare ports accept a thermometer/pH probe or reactant addition. Electrode leads connect to a separate potentiostat. Gas modes are purge, blanket and vent; no electronic command-state map is provided for the passive cell.
Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Electrode potential/current response is conveyed to the connected potentiostat; corrosion/impedance results depend on that instrument and method. The passive cell itself does not acquire or export digital measurements. Purge gas exits the vent; the reacted electrolyte/specimen remain in the cell. The unspecified inventory row does not confirm the MultiPort model or an eight-channel potentiostat.
Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>mL (MultiPort standard operating volume: 1000 mL); cm² or in² (nominal gasket-covered electrode area); mm/in (specimen geometry). Voltage, current, impedance, temperature and pH units/ranges depend on separately installed measuring instruments.
Source: H, MultiPort Cell Kit manual, PDF pp. 8, 13, 17–19, 23–26.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>12</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Gamry corrosion cell</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://www.gamry.com/assets/Uploads/MultiPort-Manual-Rev1-4.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-043">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>REQ-EQ-043</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Tracer 2.0 Mobile Platform — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Workload: payload mounted on the mobile base (rated 100 kg). Power: 24 V battery. Commands: forward/reverse linear velocity and left/right angular velocity through CAN 2.0B at 500 kbit/s or the RC handset; emergency stop must be released. Feedback modes are standby=0x00, CAN=0x01 and RC=0x02. RC takes priority over CAN. Motion-command timeout after 500 ms sets velocity to zero.
Source: H, PDF pp. 3, 7–8, 11–19, 22–26, 34.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Chassis translation/rotation; CAN feedback for actual linear/angular velocity, battery voltage, chassis/control-mode status, fault bits and motor information. Fault bits use 0=normal/no alarm and 1=fault/alarm. Feedback motor speed is in rpm; the side interface also provides 24 V expansion power.
Source: H, PDF pp. 3, 7–8, 11–19, 22–26, 34.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>mm/s (CAN linear velocity); 0.001 rad/s (CAN angular-velocity scaling); m/s (rated travel speed); rpm (motor feedback); V (battery, reported with ×10 integer scaling); A (motor current); °C (temperature); kg (payload); ms (command timing); kbit/s (CAN bitrate); coded/Boolean status flags (dimensionless)
Source: H, PDF pp. 3, 7–8, 11–19, 22–26, 34.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>3</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>AgileX Robotics Tracer 2.0 Mobile Platform</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://static.generation-robots.com/media/user-manual-tracer-2-0-agilex-robotics.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
