  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-035">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>REQ-EQ-035</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Standard Bots Thor — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Workload: end effector/workpiece within the 30 kg payload rating; six-axis motion program. Supported operating modes: collaborative or high-speed non-collaborative. Control box: 16 digital inputs and 4 analogue inputs, stated as 24 V tolerant; TCP/IP, Modbus TCP and EtherNet/IP are listed. Tool M8 8-pin connector: 2 digital inputs and 2 analogue inputs (24 V tolerant); RS-485/UART up to 10 Mbit/s. Controller supply: 90–264 VAC, 47–63 Hz; program/payload-dependent power up to 4 kW. Tool-I/O hardware is listed, but the April 2026 footnote says software support was forthcoming; confirm installed firmware. Input HIGH/LOW thresholds and analogue ranges/scaling are not specified.
Source: Manuals2/6ad0b7d901069695bb0263e1_New Thor Specs 202604.pdf, PDF p. 2.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Commanded robot/tool motion, rated reach 2 m, maximum TCP speed 4 m/s, repeatability ±0.025 mm. Control box: 16 digital outputs, 24 V / 0.7 A continuous; combined supply limit 3 A with internal power or 12 A with external power. Tool: 2 digital outputs, open-drain or push-pull (listed 1 A rating); zero analogue outputs; tool power 12/24 V, 6 A continuous maximum. The tool hardware/software-support caveat also applies to these outputs. Default states, per-pin assignments, fault/ready meanings and calibrated position/force telemetry fields are not supplied by the sheet.
Source: Manuals2/6ad0b7d901069695bb0263e1_New Thor Specs 202604.pdf, PDF p. 2.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>kg (payload); m/mm (reach, repeatability and geometry); degrees and °/s (joint range/speed); m/s (TCP speed); W/kW (power); V/VAC and A (electrical supply/I/O ratings); Hz (mains frequency); °C (temperature); %RH (humidity); Mbit/s (serial data rate). Channel counts/DOF are dimensionless. These are published operating/specification units; analogue scaling and digital logic thresholds are not given.
Source: Manuals2/6ad0b7d901069695bb0263e1_New Thor Specs 202604.pdf, PDF p. 2.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>27</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Standard Bots Thor</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://thorhelp.standardbots.com/1-introduction.html"/>
  </rdf:Description>
