  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-040">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>REQ-EQ-040</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Light Conversion CARBIDE CB1-04 — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>PARTIAL FAMILY REFERENCE — installed CB1-04 controller not verified. The manual’s safety-shutter declaration expressly includes CARBIDE CB1 among the listed families. For the documented shutter subsystem, control is by shutter switch or software; interruption of the remote-interlock circuit is abnormal and requires a manual reset or software reset to restore shutter operation. Use this as family-level safety evidence only: the exact CB1-04 power, cooling, trigger and control-pin inputs remain unestablished.
Source: Manuals2/CARBIDE-CB3-80W-User-Manual (1).pdf, PDF pp. 84–89 and 107.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>PARTIAL FAMILY REFERENCE — installed CB1-04 controller not verified. The listed safety function is emergency-stop activation on shutter failure. In the documented safety-shutter subsystem, a detected failure interrupts SHUTTER ERROR OUTPUTS; an external power-switching/emergency-stop circuit is needed to remove laser power, and shutter function is restored by a complete controller power cycle. Exact CB1-04 laser-output specifications, connector levels and status-pin mappings are not established; CB3-80W performance limits were not transferred.
Source: Manuals2/CARBIDE-CB3-80W-User-Manual (1).pdf, PDF pp. 84–89 and 107.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>CPA-based Yb:KGW Femtosecond / Picosecond Laser; 1028 nm – 1030 nm; Tunable from 290 fs to 10 ps; Pulse energy &gt; 100 µJ; Repetition rate 100 kHz to 1000 kHz; Power requirements 110 to 220 VAC, 50/60 Hz (up to 300 W max draw);</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>14</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Light Conversion CARBIDE CB1-04</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://lightcon.com/wp-content/uploads/datasheets/LC-Scientific-Interface-Module-for-CARBIDE-260601.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
