  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-05%3Aoutputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Output and output states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>outputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>RS-232 commands and responses: 300/1200/2400/9600/19200 baud; up to 100 pumps; states: Commands RUN/STP/PUR; DIS/VER/IN queries; status/error responses; basic or safe communications mode
Dispensed/withdrawn material: Flow follows the configured direction and syringe-dependent rate; states: Infusing, withdrawing or stopped; phase: Fluid; phase/composition depends on loaded sample
Program output, pin 5: User/program-defined logic output; states: LOW or HIGH; OUT 5 {0|1}
Motor-running output, pin 7: RUN.0 or RUN.1 mapping; states: RUN.0 HIGH=pumping, LOW=not pumping; RUN.1 HIGH=pumping or pause timer, LOW=program stopped/paused
Direction output, pin 8: Logic direction indication; states: HIGH=infuse; LOW=withdraw
Dispensed-volume/status response: DIS reports dispensed volume; firmware/status responses available through RS-232; states: Separate infuse/withdraw counters; status responses depend on command and pump state
Buzzer: BUZ controls audible notification; states: Off, continuous, or specified number of beeps</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-05"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M50-09%3Aoutputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Output and output states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>outputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Agitated/mixed sample; uniformity or particle size is not guaranteed by the instrument description. Family document; numeric limits/options must be checked for this variant.
Source: Manuals/30392115-manual.pdf, PDF p. 1.</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M50-09"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-042%3Aoutputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Output and output states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>outputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Control-box analog outputs: Voltage mode 0–10 V or current mode 4–20 mA; 12-bit resolution; states: Voltage/current output mode selected; range and load constraints apply
Control-box digital outputs: PNP; current 0–1 A with specified loads; states: HIGH/LOW; voltage drop and leakage limits given in manual
Tool digital outputs: Sinking NPN, sourcing PNP or push/pull; states: NPN active=LOW/inactive=open; PNP active=HIGH/inactive=open; push/pull active=HIGH/inactive=LOW; emergency stop=high impedance
Tool power supply: Selectable 0/12/24 V; specified single-/dual-pin current limits; states: Off, 12 V or 24 V; dual-pin mode changes output-pin availability
Tool/workpiece motion: Six-joint robot motion within configured workspace; states: Trajectory and stop conditions are program/safety-configuration dependent; phase: Workpiece phase is not prescribed</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-042"/>
  </rdf:Description>
