  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M07-08%3Ainputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Input and input states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>inputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Liquid in one or two syringes; syringe type, inside diameter and volume; infusion/withdrawal rate; target volume. Legato 210 (788210) supports infuse only, withdraw only, infuse/withdraw, withdraw/infuse and continuous modes, and stores one program. Target time is available in infusion-only or withdrawal-only mode. Supply: 100–240 VAC, 50–60 Hz. USB/RS-232 ASCII commands control run/stop and infusion/withdrawal settings. Family 15-pin I/O: direction input rising edge = infuse, falling edge = refill; footswitch can toggle run/stop or start/stop on configured edges; trigger input is TTL high/low. Listed input thresholds: HIGH ≥2 V, LOW ≤0.4 V. Multi-program/advanced 210P features and the 0–10 V analog-input option listed only for 788212/788272 are not assigned to the standard 210. Installed controller/firmware applicability must be checked.
Source: Manuals/KDS Legato 200 Series_5617-002REV2.0.pdf, PDF pp. 6, 8, 11, 17–19, 62–65, 79, 89. Model scope: Legato 210 (788210).</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M07-08"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M17-02%3Ainputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Input and input states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>inputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Materials/workload: Sample to be freeze-dried; refrigeration/vacuum and collector connections as specified.
Other per-input states/guards: not established by this functional summary.
Sources: H PDF pp. 1.</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M17-02"/>
  </rdf:Description>
