    <icon:scope>UHV RF atom-source components for atomic species deposition/cleaning; not turnkey vacuum systems. Manufacturer product claims only. P/N links express curator relevance, not source-article apparatus, measured performance, exact host compatibility or mandatory process steps. TAS atom brochure pages 2 and 4 identify the 60 mm aperture variant. Neutral-atom source for a compatible host, distinct from the ion-source series. P19 relevance is specifically an optional nitride-PLD configuration; not apparatus from the cited P19 experiment. P46 relevance does not establish a replacement for UCLA installed hardware. Manufacturer operating envelopes are not recipe setpoints. Public purchase price and exact-model operating manual were not published in this bounded review. No documented successor relationship or newest-generation claim. No make/model match in the user-designated Purdue list; generic PVD wording is not asset identity.</icon:scope>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/evidence_registry.csv"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://therisnano.com/rf-atom-sources/"/>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://therisnano.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/TAS-Brochure-2023.pdf"/>
    <dct:source rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/evidence-source/CAT-EV-9FE3BAFFE3F0333A%3A1"/>
