  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/M23-09">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/ontology#InputOutputProfile"/>
    <dct:identifier>M23-09</dct:identifier>
    <rdfs:label>Denton Discovery 18 — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Substrate and sputter targets; process-gas supply, vacuum-pump connections and RF/DC sputtering power. The brochure lists two 2-inch magnetron cathodes with independent shutters, 500 W RF and 1 kW DC supplies, and substrate rotation adjustable from 0 to 25 rpm. A microprocessor PLC controls vacuum valves and auto-pump/auto-vent sequencing with software interlocks. The optional DVO/CS automation package is not assumed installed.
Source: Manuals/Discovery-18.pdf, PDF pp. 1 and 4, visually reviewed.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Sputtered coating on the substrate; digital mass-flow and vacuum-pressure readouts. Valve/pump/vent and shutter operation are described, but the brochure does not enumerate the electrical ready/alarm/pin-state map.
Source: Manuals/Discovery-18.pdf, PDF pp. 1 and 4, visually reviewed.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>Torr (vacuum pressure); L/s and cfm (pumping speed); rpm (substrate rotation); W/kW (RF/DC power); V and A (DC supply rating); in (target/substrate geometry).
Source: Manuals/Discovery-18.pdf, PDF pp. 1 and 4, visually reviewed.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>270</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Denton Discovery 18</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
  </rdf:Description>
