  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/REQ-EQ-009%3Aoutputs_and_states">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://schema.org/PropertyValue"/>
    <schema:name>Output and output states</schema:name>
    <schema:propertyID>outputs_and_states</schema:propertyID>
    <schema:value>Deposited metal part. In the documented L2 sensing configuration, logged outputs include elapsed program time, layer number, infill/contour flags, feed velocity, XYZ/A/C position, laser power, melt-pool diameter, enclosure temperature, powder-disc speed and gas flows. Melt-pool sensing requires the study’s installed monitoring hardware; later CT porosity is an external test, not an L2 output.
Source: H, Hespeler et al., Applied Sciences 12 (2022), 8974, PDF pp. 7–9 and Table 1.</schema:value>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-io/REQ-EQ-009"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://github.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/id/equipment-property/M42-04%3Aoutputs_and_states">
