    <rdfs:label>Topas DDU 570/L — input/output metadata</rdfs:label>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:resource="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PodComet/ICoN-PCL-Equipment-Metadata/main/catalog/equipment_io.csv"/>
    <icon:inputDescription>Aerosol stream and silica-gel desiccant in the DDU 570/L; ambient-pressure operation, not overpressure service. Desiccant state: orange=dry/usable, pale colourless=loaded and to be replaced/regenerated.
Source: I, German datasheet, PDF pp. 1–2.</icon:inputDescription>
    <icon:outputDescription>Dried aerosol stream; no direct contact between aerosol and desiccant. Desiccant colour provides the listed qualitative saturation indication; no electrical/data signal outputs are specified.
Source: I, German datasheet, PDF pp. 1–2.</icon:outputDescription>
    <icon:measuringUnitsDescription>°C (ambient/aerosol temperature); g (desiccant mass); mm (hose connection). Flow/measurement display units are not stated for this variant.
Source: I, German datasheet, PDF pp. 1–2.</icon:measuringUnitsDescription>
    <icon:sourceSha256>c22c4681926fb5b28876a7db7c55d9e527e4ad9fada4ab8774b9aa2b9538bcab</icon:sourceSha256>
    <icon:sourceSheet>Sheet1</icon:sourceSheet>
    <icon:sourceRow>1028</icon:sourceRow>
    <icon:sourceModel>Topas DDU 570/L</icon:sourceModel>
    <icon:importedDate>2026-10-30</icon:importedDate>
    <dct:references rdf:resource="https://www.topas-gmbh.de/fileadmin/user_upload/Produkte/documents/products/sheets/DE/topas-570-DDU-productsheet-de.pdf"/>
  </rdf:Description>
